        "A recurring trap in this space is assuming a token proves more than it actually does. An NFT proves that a specific wallet controls a specific entry in a specific smart contract — full stop. Whether that entry corresponds honestly to a real ticket, a real membership, or a real physical object depends entirely on whoever set the system up, and whether they did so honestly and competently.",
